---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;

---
<BaseLayout title="Our Work">
Our work spans recovery and reconstruction after disasters, 
ecological stewardship, people-centred urban development, and 
institutional strengthening. Across these areas, we work with 
communities, governments, universities and development partners to 
create practical, locally grounded solutions.

<section class="theme-section ecology">
    <img
    src={`${base}images/themes/ecological-balance.jpg`}
    alt="Ecological Balance"
    class="theme-image"
    />

  <div class="theme-content">

    <h2>Restructuring Human Interventions for Ecological Balance</h2>
     <p class="theme-geographies">
     India
    </p>

    <p>
     Human interventions have brought us close to destruction through 
     resource exploitation and system collapse. As climate change 
     accelerates and natural resources—especially water—face severe 
     scarcity, human development must adapt. We critically evaluate and 
     redesign interventions to promote environmental sustainability, 
     resource revitalization, and social equity. By centering community 
     rights, water governance, and adaptive management, our work bridges 
     technical aspects with inclusive policy frameworks—enabling 
     ecosystems and local communities to thrive together. Our partners 
     include the International Water Management Institute, Aga Khan Rural 
     Support Programme, Tata Trusts, WAPCOS, and Ambuja Foundation. 
    </p>

    <h3>Range of Work</h3>
    <p class="theme-services">
       Ecological resources planning · Implementation guidelines ·
       Policy analysis and advisory support · Technical guidelines · Capacity building
    </p>
 
    <a
      href={`${base}work/ecological-balance/`}
      class="theme-button"
    >
      View Projects
    </a>

  </div>
  
   
</section>

<section class="theme-section resilience">

  <div class="theme-content">

    <h2>Reinforcing People's Resilience to Disasters</h2>
    <p class="theme-geographies">
     India | Nepal | Afghanistan | Indonesia | Myanmar | Somalia | Mozambique
    </p>

    <p>
      Natural hazards pose significant risks to our well being. The 
      risks are particularly high for the poor and vulnerable. 
      People’s capacities need to be reinforced for disaster risk 
      mitigation and management. This thematic area focuses on 
      mainstreaming disaster risk management into development planning,  
      specific risk mitigation planning, post-disaster reconstruction 
      and recovery.  Our key partners include National Disaster Management 
      Authority (NDMA), Gujarat State Management Authority (GSDMA), 
      Gujarat Institute of Disaster Management (GIDM), UNDP, 
      Canadian International Development Agency (CIDA), 
      Owner Driven Reconstruction Collaborative (ODRC), Earthquake 
      Engineering Research Institute (EERI), Hunnarshala, and UNNATI.
     </p>

    <h3>Range of Work</h3>
    <p class="theme-services">
       Post-disaster needs assessment · Recovery planning and facilitation · 
       Policy support  · Technical guidelines · Capacity building · Monitoring
       and evaluation
	</p>
   

    <a
      href={`${base}work/resilience/`}
      class="theme-button"
    >
      View Projects
    </a>

  </div>
  
    <img
    src={`${base}images/themes/resilience.jpg`}
    alt="Resilience"
    class="theme-image"
    />  

</section>

<section class="theme-section urban">
    <img
    src={`${base}images/themes/urban-space.jpg`}
    alt="Reclaiming Urban Space"
    class="theme-image"
    />

  <div class="theme-content">

    <h2>Reclaiming Urban Space for the People</h2>
     <p class="theme-geographies">
     India
    </p>

    <p>
      Urban space has been usurped by the market. The informal 
      workers and dwellers have no ownership and protection. The urban 
      space is no more humane. This thematic area focuses on issues of 
      urban planning and development with an idea to work towards making 
      cities for its people. We provide research, planning, monitoring 
      and evaluation services. Our partners include Municipal 
      Corporations, NGOs and local communities. 
    </p>

    <h3>Range of Work</h3>
    <p class="theme-services">
       Ecological resources planning · Implementation guidelines ·
       Policy analysis and advisory support · Technical guidelines · Capacity building
    </p>
 
    <a
      href={`${base}work/urban-space/`}
      class="theme-button"
    >
      View Projects
    </a>

  </div>
  
   
</section>

<section class="theme-section capacity">

  <div class="theme-content">

    <h2>Re-grounding Research in Socio-Economic Community Realities</h2>
    <p class="theme-geographies">
     In-person: India
    </p>
     <p class="theme-geographies">
     Online: Africa | Latin America | South East Asia | Europe | North America
    </p>

    <p>
      Traditional academic curricula often fall short of equipping young 
      researchers and practitioners with the socio economic field-based 
      realities of development, economics, technology, and governance. 
      We facilitate alternative educational programs, certificate courses, 
      and practical research platforms that take learning beyond college 
      classrooms. By mentoring students and emerging scholars in 
      field-anchored socio-economic research with interdisciplinary 
      analysis, we nurture a new generation of researchers capable of 
      tackling real-world social and developmental challenges. Our partners 
      include International Development Economics Associates (IDEAs).
     </p>

    <h3>Range of Work</h3>
    <p class="theme-services">
       Facilitation and management of certificate course 
	</p>
   

    <a
      href={`${base}work/institutional-initiatives/`}
      class="theme-button"
    >
      View Projects
    </a>

  </div>
  
    <img
    src={`${base}images/themes/resilience.jpg`}
    alt="Resilience"
    class="theme-image"
    />  

</section>

</BaseLayout>
